{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The original J-B Weld epoxy felt useful because it could complement the nails, screws, and anchors I have been buying for practical repairs.",
    "That general repair adhesive connected with my recent maintenance needs without requiring a specialized project."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The feeler gauge, metal-cutting wheels, and thread-cutting kit serve tasks I have not shown a current need for; buying fasteners does not mean I need every workshop tool.",
    "Marine epoxy, silicone sealant, and waterproof glue assume specific bonding or sealing jobs I do not currently have. Water-testing equipment and a thermometer were even less connected to my recent needs.",
    "The clear glue felt redundant once I had chosen the repair epoxy; I do not currently need several different adhesives."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My purchases seemed to be treated as broad interest in tools and repair supplies, although the repeated need was fastening and mounting.",
    "The list leaned heavily on adhesives and waterproof products without evidence that I have multiple bonding jobs or a water-related repair."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The repeated nails, wood screws, and drywall anchors suggest that the intended task and compatible materials matter more to me than a general connection to repair work.",
    "My medicine cups and replacement vacuum bags reflect separate practical needs; they do not establish an interest in measuring instruments or general equipment.",
    "I choose supplies when I can connect them to a current job, so specialized products need a clearer reason than simply being useful around a workshop."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my practical repair needs but stretched them into unsupported specialized tasks and too many adhesive options."
}"}
